Here are the exact replacements to fix the scrolling issue in the preview table and make the black text highly readable in the error alert by adjusting its background color.
### 1. Fix the Table Scroll
Find the tableContainerStyle object near the top of your file (around line 63). The issue is that overflow is set to "hidden", which disables scrolling entirely.
**Find this block:**
```javascript
const tableContainerStyle = {
  borderRadius: "12px",
  border: "1px solid",
  borderColor: "divider",
  overflow: "hidden",
  marginTop: "20px",
  boxShadow: 1,
  maxHeight: 600,
};

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
const tableContainerStyle = {
  borderRadius: "12px",
  border: "1px solid",
  borderColor: "divider",
  overflowY: "auto", // Forces vertical scrollbar when data exceeds maxHeight
  marginTop: "20px",
  boxShadow: 1,
  maxHeight: 600,
};

```
### 2. Fix the Error Alert Visibility
Find the Alert component rendering the error message (around line 348, inside activeStep === 0). We will keep the text color black, but change the background to a very light, soft pink/red (#ffebee) so the text stands out clearly.
**Find this block:**
```javascript
            {resultStatus === "ERROR" && (
              <Alert severity="error" sx={{ mt: 3, mx: "auto", maxWidth: "100%" }}>
                {resultMsg} — {downloadMsg}
              </Alert>
            )}

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
            {resultStatus === "ERROR" && (
              <Alert 
                severity="error" 
                sx={{ 
                  mt: 3, 
                  mx: "auto", 
                  maxWidth: "100%",
                  backgroundColor: "#ffebee", // Very light red background
                  color: "black",             // Explicitly black text
                  "& .MuiAlert-icon": {
                    color: "error.main"       // Keeps the icon dark red
                  }
                }}
              >
                {resultMsg} — {downloadMsg}
              </Alert>
            )}

```
